Subject: movsx from bp and sp sign-extends

movsx from the 16-bit registers bp and sp was emitted as a zero extension. Bink's integer IDCT
(005B45B0) loads a coefficient into bp and sign-extends it later, so negative coefficients
corrupted the intro movie and the title background.

---
diff --git a/tools/recomp/lifter.py b/tools/recomp/lifter.py
--- a/tools/recomp/lifter.py
+++ b/tools/recomp/lifter.py
@@ -1825,7 +1825,7 @@
             r = ops[1].reg
             if r in ("al", "bl", "cl", "dl", "ah", "bh", "ch", "dh"):
                 src = f"SX8({src})"
-            elif r in ("ax", "bx", "cx", "dx", "si", "di"):
+            elif r in ("ax", "bx", "cx", "dx", "si", "di", "bp", "sp"):
                 src = f"SX16({src})"
         return [_fmt_operand_write(ops[0], src)]
 
